Z||000004||Monkeyman||10-31-2001||01:22 AM||||Whatever you do, <B>make sure you don't let your wires get cut!!!</B>||||reg||1
Z||000005||AgaricX||10-31-2001||01:37 AM||||Thick rubber tubing's a must.  Cut wires = bad.||||reg||1
Z||000006||MrPBody||10-31-2001||09:02 AM||||<A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com" TARGET=_blank>V8 Archie</A> has a fiberglass battery tray, and <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com/" TARGET=_blank>West Coast Fiero</A> has an aluminum tray.  Or you could make your own.<P>(Edit) Never mind, you already made your tray.  <I>One of these days, I'll learn to read!</I><BR><p>[This message has been edited by MrPBody (edited 10-31-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||artherd||11-01-2001||05:04 AM||||I ran my wires *inside* grey electrical conduit...  that should stand up to a lot of abuse. <P>You do NOT want to try to arc weld your full gas tank....<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000008||DrDave||11-01-2001||09:59 PM||||    I'm getting ready to run my battery cable pretty soon, but I havn't made up my mind what I'm going to use to insulate it.  If ya really pinched it would the rubber burn, Yes, the grey plastic conduit probably, but then if ya got in that bad an accident, You'd be in a Bunch of trouble anyway.   Ain't it always somthine in the way?||||reg||1
